---
layout: base
---
{% from "macros/section-bar.njk" import sectionBar %}
{% set pageSubtitle = subtitle or (navigation.items | getDescription(permalink)) %}

{# The list-shaped index pages are headed by a section bar; prose pages keep
   the title and subtitle treatment. #}
<article class="page">
    {%- if listPage %}
    {{ sectionBar(title, barLink, barHref, 1) }}
    {%- else %}
    <header class="page-header">
        <h1 class="page-title">{{ title }}</h1>
        {% if pageSubtitle %}
        <div class="page-subtitle">{{ pageSubtitle }}</div>
        {% endif %}
        {#
            When a page is worth dating, the date is a line of reference under
            the header — the same tracked caps a post opens with — rather than
            a boxed aside beside it. It is opt-in, because on most pages here
            the fact is noise: a colophon is not truer for having been edited
            last week.

            `lastUpdated` wins over `page.date` where it is given. `page.date`
            is git's last-modified, which moves whenever any commit touches the
            file, so a typo fix or a site-wide restyle restamps a page whose
            content has not changed in a year. The sitemap prefers the same
            field for the same reason.
        #}
        {%- if showUpdated %}
        {%- set updated = lastUpdated or page.date %}
        <p class="page-updated">Updated <time datetime="{{ updated | w3Date }}">{{ updated | htmlDate }}</time></p>
        {%- endif %}
    </header>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="page-content">
        {{ content | safe }}
    </div>
</article>
